# A battle shown in a window with a computer player of a mod on one side (docs/sdk/ai-protocol.md
# §8): with seed 7 (6 until the computer players' minister rules of 2026-10-14), ten systems
# and seven empires, after the computer has played every empire for 40 turns (the computer
# empires by the fixture mod's Captain, which notes its first ship in every combat turn), the
# player's first End Turn stops at a battle in a computer player's turn.
# Strategic fights it in the Strategic Combat window, where Captain gives its side's orders each
# combat turn as in the engine's own battles; Close lets the turn go on with those answers (the
# window's players let the script runtime go first: nothing fails), and the AI notes view lists
# Captain's notes, its battle notes among them.
# layouts: both (also plays at 800x600: run_input_tests.py --small)
options --mods-dir=tests/fixtures/mods --mod=test.ai-fixture --ai=test.ai-fixture:Captain --quick-start --seed=7 --systems=10 --empires=7 --turns=40 --open=none --layout=1024x768 --size=1280x800

wait-screen game
assert-turn 40
repeat 10
  click item:"*(suggested)" optional timeout=5
end
click tag:button:end-turn
click item:Yes in="End Turn" optional
wait-for item:Begin timeout=1800
click item:Begin
wait-window strategic-combat
click item:Strategic in=strategic-combat
wait 20
screenshot battle-window.png
wait 300
assert-enabled item:Close in=strategic-combat
click item:Close in=strategic-combat
wait-closed strategic-combat
# Other battles the turn stops at, if any: each fought strategically too.
repeat 4
  click item:Begin optional timeout=240
  click item:Strategic in=strategic-combat optional timeout=30
  wait 300
  click item:Close in=strategic-combat optional timeout=30
end
wait-turn 41
# The Log opens once the turn's moves have been shown.
wait-window log
key Escape
wait-closed log
assert-absent item:"player-failure:*"
key Ctrl+Shift+N
wait-for item:"ai-note:*fighting, combat turn*"
screenshot battle-notes.png
